    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Pathogenesis of cribriform-morular thyroid carcinoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Under normal conditions, in the absence of WNT binding to Frizzled receptors, &beta;-catenin interacts with the destruction complex (CK1, GSK3B, APC, and AXIN1), resulting in its phosphorylation by CK1 and GSK3B and its subsequent degradation by the proteasome. In sporadic cribriform-morular thyroid carcinoma, somatic mutations in <em>APC</em>, <em>CTNNB1</em>, and/or <em>AXIN1</em> alter the destruction complex, impairing &beta;-catenin phosphorylation and degradation. &beta;-Catenin accumulates in the cytoplasm and subsequently translocates to the nucleus, where it acts as an activator of TCF/LEF proteins that lead to the constitutive expression of WNT target genes. In cribriform-morular thyroid carcinomas associated with familial adenomatous polyposis, there are germline <em>APC</em> mutations.",
    "source": "José Manuel Cameselle-Teijeiro",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/53/55/25806.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/53/55/thumb_25806.jpg"
  },
